tsproxy (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * -hostname is optional; it defaults to the first label of the target
    host.
  * tsproxy@.service takes the target as its instance name
    (tsproxy@host:port) and no longer needs ~/.config/tsproxy/NAME.env.
    The file is optional, read as ~/.config/tsproxy/INSTANCE.env.
  * Remove After=network.target from the user unit, where it did nothing.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:47:02 -0800

tsproxy (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Package for Debian: /usr/bin/tsproxy and a tsproxy@.service systemd
    user unit.
  * tsproxy@.service reads the target address from
    ~/.config/tsproxy/NAME.env instead of hardcoding it.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:22:05 -0800
